e expérimentalement confirmée ;\n","• l’origine physique d’un champ temporel privilégié u^mu ;\n","• une dynamique unique de ce champ ;\n","• une déviation observée par rapport à la relativité générale.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","SOURCE-MATCHING-LAYER-ESTABLISHED / PHYSICAL-TIMELIKE-ORIGIN-NOT-YET-DERIVED.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","2. 0.2.23.1 — Weak Field Coefficient Extraction for PPN\n","\n","Résultat mathématique figé\n","\n","Pour la famille statique paramétrique, le notebook utilise :\n","\n","$$\n","\\gamma_{\\rm GVH}=\\frac{b_1}{a_1},\n","\\qquad\n","\\beta_{\\rm GVH}=\\frac{a_2}{a_1^2}.\n","$$\n","\n","La séparation méthodologique est essentielle : les interfaces\n","phénoménologiques de type\n","\n","$$\n","\\gamma_{\\rm eff}=1+\\epsilon_D\\gamma_D,\n","\\qquad\n","\\beta_{\\rm eff}=1+\\epsilon_D\\beta_D\n","$$\n","\n","ne sont pas, à elles seules, des prédictions dynamiques GVH. Les\n","coefficients doivent provenir de la solution statique/source-matching.\n","\n","À premier ordre, avec\n","\n","$$\n","a_1=1+\\epsilon_D\\alpha_1,\\quad\n","a_2=1+\\epsilon_D\\alpha_2,\\quad\n","b_1=1+\\epsilon_D\\sigma_1,\n","$$\n","\n","on obtient\n","\n","$$\n","\\gamma_{\\rm GVH}-1\n","=\\epsilon_D(\\sigma_1-\\alpha_1)+\\mathcal O(\\epsilon_D^2),\n","$$\n","\n","$$\n","\\beta_{\\rm GVH}-1\n","=\\epsilon_D(\\alpha_2-2\\alpha_1)+\\mathcal O(\\epsilon_D^2).\n","$$\n","\n","Ce qui est réellement démontré\n","\n","La carte entre coefficients métriques faibles et paramètres PPN est\n","dérivée pour la famille statique paramétrique.\n","\n","Ce qui reste hypothétique\n","\n","Une valeur non triviale de gamma_GVH-1 ou beta_GVH-1 n’est pas\n","établie simplement parce que cette paramétrisation existe. Il faut que\n","la dynamique GVH fixe indépendamment les coefficients concernés.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","PASS-WEAK-FIELD-COEFFICIENT-MAP / NO-INDEPENDENT-NON-GR-PREDICTION-YET.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","3. 0.2.23.2 — Covariant Source Projector Derivation\n","\n","Résultat mathématique figé\n","\n","Le notebook définit le projecteur spatial\n","\n","$$\n","h_{\\mu\\nu}=g_{\\mu\\nu}+u_\\mu u_\\nu,\n","\\qquad\n","u^\\mu u_\\mu=-1,\n","$$\n","\n","où la seconde relation doit être lue comme la contrainte de\n","normalisation de u^mu :\n","\n","$$\n","u^\\mu u_\\mu=-1.\n","$$\n","\n","Le projecteur symétrique spatial sans trace est\n","\n","$$ \\mathcal P_{\\mu\\nu}{}^{\\alpha\\beta}\n","\n","h_{(\\mu}{}^\\alpha h_{\\nu)}{}^\\beta\n","-\\frac13 h_{\\mu\\nu}h^{\\alpha\\beta},\n","$$\n","\n","et\n","\n","$$ \\Pi_{\\mu\\nu}[T]\n","\n","\\mathcal P_{\\mu\\nu}{}^{\\alpha\\beta}T_{\\alpha\\beta}.\n","$$\n","\n","Pour la décomposition\n","\n","$$\n","T_{\\mu\\nu}=\\rho u_\\mu u_\\nu+p h_{\\mu\\nu}\n","+2u_{(\\mu}q_{\\nu)}+\\pi_{\\mu\\nu},\n","$$\n","\n","la chaîne identifie\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{\\Pi_{\\mu\\nu}[T]=\\pi_{\\mu\\nu}}.\n","$$\n","\n","Ainsi ce canal sélectionne le stress anisotrope, et non directement\n","la densité isotrope ou la pression isotrope.\n","\n","Verrou découvert\n","\n","La définition du projecteur suppose déjà un champ temporel unitaire\n","u^mu. Le projecteur ne fournit donc pas, par lui-même, l’origine\n","physique de u^mu.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","PASS-COVARIANT-STF-PROJECTOR / TIMELIKE-FIELD-ORIGIN-OPEN.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","4. 0.2.23.3.1 — Timelike Field Dynamics and Covariant Closure\n","\n","Pourquoi 0.2.23.3.1 est canonique\n","\n","0.2.23.3.1 remplace la dépendance défectueuse de 0.2.23.3 sans\n","changer la question scientifique centrale. La version corrigée audite\n","explicitement la provenance des notebooks nécessaires.\n","\n","Question physique\n","\n","Le champ\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{u^\\mu}\n","$$\n","\n","est-il :\n","\n","• la quadrivitesse de la matière ;\n","• un objet géométrique dérivé ;\n","• un champ dynamique indépendant ?\n","\n","La contrainte\n","\n","$$\n","u^\\mu u_\\mu=-1\n","$$\n","\n","peut être imposée covariamment, mais cela ne sélectionne pas à lui seul\n","la dynamique physique du champ.\n","\n","Ce que le notebook établit\n","\n","Il formalise les conditions nécessaires à une fermeture covariante et\n","distingue : fermeture cinématique, contrainte unitaire, dynamique\n","timelike unique et fermeture covariante complète.\n","\n","Ce qu’il ne doit pas faire\n","\n","Ajouter arbitrairement une action ou choisir un modèle uniquement parce\n","qu’il ferme les équations.\n","\n","La sortie logique de cette étape est donc : si les postulats antérieurs\n","ne sélectionnent pas une dynamique unique, la sélection doit être\n","traitée explicitement dans l’étape suivante.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","COVARIANT-CLOSURE-STRUCTURE-DEFINED / UNIQUE-TIMELIKE-DYNAMICS-NOT-DERIVED.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","5. 0.2.23.4.1 — Timelike Field Model Selection and Falsifiability\n","\n","Modèles comparés\n","\n","A — quadrivitesse de la matière\n","\n","$$\n","u^\\mu=u^\\mu_{\\rm matter}.\n","$$\n","\n","B — gradient scalaire normalisé\n","\n","$$\n","u_\\mu=-\\frac{\\nabla_\\mu\\phi}\n","{\\sqrt{-\\nabla_\\alpha\\phi\\nabla^\\alpha\\phi}}.\n","$$\n","\n","C — champ vectoriel unitaire indépendant\n","\n","Le champ u^mu devient alors un degré de liberté fondamental\n","supplémentaire soumis à une contrainte unitaire et à une dynamique\n","propre.\n","\n","Résultat figé\n","\n","La comparaison technique de ces trois classes ne fournit pas une\n","sélection physique unique à partir des postulats GVH actuels.\n","\n","La version 0.2.23.4.1 corrige la traçabilité vers 0.2.23.3.1 ; la\n","logique scientifique, les calculs et le verdict sont conservés.\n","\n","Les statuts de gouvernance pertinents sont :\n","\n","```text\n","PASS-MODEL-CLASSIFICATION-NO-UNIQUE-SELECTION\n","BLOCKED-NO-UNIQUE-MODEL-FROM-CURRENT-POSTULATES\n","NEW-FALSIFIABLE-POSTULATE-REQUIRED\n","```\n","\n","Interprétation\n","\n","C’est un résultat négatif utile : la chaîne empêche une sélection ad\n","hoc.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","NO-UNIQUE-SELECTION / NEW-FALSIFIABLE-POSTULATE-REQUIRED.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","6. 0.2.23.5.1 — Timelike Field Physical Postulate and Origin\n","\n","Question finale de la sous-chaîne\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{u^\\mu\\ \\text{peut-il être dérivé d’une structure GVH existante ?}}\n","$$\n","\n","Origines candidates examinées\n","\n","1. direction temporelle propre de l’observateur ;\n","2. gradient d’un champ scalaire d’horloge ;\n","3. vecteur propre temporel principal d’un tenseur GVH ;\n","4. quadrivitesse de la matière ;\n","5. champ vectoriel indépendant ajouté par postulat.\n","\n","Critères d’acceptation\n","\n","Une origine n’est considérée comme physiquement dérivée que si elle\n","fournit simultanément :\n","\n","• u^mu u_mu = -1 ;\n","• une définition covariante ;\n","• une direction unique dans le vide et dans la matière ;\n","• une limite GR contrôlée ;\n","• au moins une conséquence falsifiable.\n","\n","Une construction mathématiquement possible n’est donc pas assimilée à\n","une dérivation physique.\n","\n","Résultat consolidé\n","\n","La chaîne identifie des candidats, mais aucune origine physique unique\n","n’est dérivée.\n","\n","```text\n","PASS-CANDIDATE-TIMELIKE-ORIGINS-IDENTIFIED\n","BLOCKED-UNIQUE-PHYSICAL-ORIGIN\n","NEW-PHYSICAL-POSTULATE-REQUIRED\n","```\n","\n","L’artefact final retient notamment deux pistes :\n","\n","• candidat GVH natif : vecteur propre timelike normalisé d’un tenseur\n","D^mu_nu ;\n","• candidat de temps directionnel : gradient normalisé d’un scalaire\n","covariant tau_G.\n","\n","Le postulat candidat enregistré est\n","\n","```text\n","P-GVH-TIME-1\n","accepted = False\n","```\n","\n","avec la forme candidate\n","\n","$$\n","u_\\mu=\n","-\\frac{\\nabla_\\mu\\tau_G}\n","{\\sqrt{-\\nabla_\\alpha\\tau_G\\nabla^\\alpha\\tau_G}}.\n","$$\n","\n","Il n’est pas accepté à ce stade.\n","\n","Points bloquants explicitement conservés\n","\n","• tau_G n’est pas encore un scalaire dynamique covariant dérivé ;\n","• D_{mu nu} ne garantit pas encore un vecteur propre timelike unique\n",";\n","• aucun candidat ne possède encore une action complète dérivée de GVH\n",";\n","• la régularité de la limite GR reste à établir.\n","\n","La construction par vecteur propre est en particulier insuffisante si le\n","tenseur s’annule, si ses valeurs propres sont dégénérées ou si aucune\n","dynamique ne garantit une valeur propre timelike unique.\n","\n","Statut consolidé :\n","CANDIDATES-IDENTIFIED / UNIQUE-PHYSICAL-ORIGIN-BLOCKED.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","7. Matrice de consolidation\n","\n","────────\n","\n","Notebook          Acquis            Non acquis          Statut figé\n","\n","────────\n","\n","0.2.23            couche covariante origine de u^mu,  SOURCE-MATCHING-LAYER\n","de source         nouvelle prédiction\n","matching utilisée expérimentale\n","par la chaîne\n","\n","0.2.23.1          carte             déviation PPN       PASS-WEAK-FIELD-MAP\n","coefficients      non-GR indépendante\n","faibles →\n","gamma_GVH,\n","beta_GVH\n","\n","0.2.23.2          projecteur STF    origine/dynamique   PASS-COVARIANT-PROJECTOR\n","covariant ; canal de u^mu\n","anisotrope\n","\n","0.2.23.3.1        structure de      dynamique timelike  UNIQUE-DYNAMICS-BLOCKED\n","fermeture et      unique\n","contraintes de\n","cohérence\n","\n","0.2.23.4.1        classification de sélection physique  NEW-FALSIFIABLE-POSTULATE-REQUIRED\n","trois modèles     unique\n","candidats\n","\n","0.2.23.5.1        candidats         origine physique    BLOCKED-UNIQUE-PHYSICAL-ORIGIN d’origine         unique identifiés et critères d’acceptation\n","\n","────────\n","\n","8. Ce que la chaîne 0.2.23 → 0.2.23.5.1 démontre globalement\n","\n","La conclusion autorisée est :\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{\n","\\text{la structure covariante peut être prolongée jusqu’au problème de }u^\\mu,\n","\\text{ mais les postulats actuels ne déterminent pas son origine physique unique.}\n","}\n","$$\n","\n","La chaîne a donc transformé une ambiguïté implicite en un verrou\n","scientifique explicite et falsifiable.\n","\n","Elle ne démontre pas :\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{\\text{GVH est une théorie gravitationnelle validée remplaçant la RG}}\n","$$\n","\n","et elle ne démontre pas encore :\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{\\text{une nouvelle prédiction gravitationnelle distincte de la RG}}\n","$$\n","\n","pour le secteur timelike considéré ici.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","9. Prochaine hypothèse physique : règle avant toute adoption\n","\n","La prochaine étape ne doit pas commencer par « choisir le candidat\n","préféré ». Elle doit commencer par définir un postulat qui risque\n","réellement d’échouer.\n","\n","Le candidat déjà archivé P-GVH-TIME-1 peut servir de cible de travail\n",":\n","\n","$$\n","\\boxed{\n","u_\\mu=-\\frac{\\nabla_\\mu\\tau_G}\n","{\\sqrt{-\\nabla_\\alpha\\tau_G\\nabla^\\alpha\\tau_G}}}\n","$$\n","\n","mais seulement si tau_G est d’abord défini comme objet covariant\n","dynamique et si ses équations ne sont pas ajustées après comparaison aux\n","observations.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","10. Critères de réfutation de la prochaine hypothèse\n","\n","Cette section distingue les critères logiques imposés par la chaîne\n","des observables concrètes à dériver dans le prochain notebook. Les\n","notebooks audités n’ont pas encore fourni une observable numérique\n","finale unique pour P-GVH-TIME-1 ; il serait donc incorrect d’en\n","inventer une ici.\n","\n","Falsificateur théorique immédiat F1 — absence de direction timelike\n","\n","Si une solution physiquement admissible produit\n","\n","$$\n","\\nabla_\\mu\\tau_G\\nabla^\\mu\\tau_G\\ge 0,\n","$$\n","\n","alors le gradient n’est pas timelike et la normalisation proposée ne\n","définit plus le champ physique voulu.\n","\n","Conséquence : P-GVH-TIME-1 est réfuté dans ce domaine, sauf si le\n","postulat avait explicitement limité son domaine avant le test.\n","\n","Falsificateur théorique F2 — non-unicité\n","\n","Si les mêmes données physiques et mêmes conditions aux limites\n","permettent plusieurs directions u^mu physiquement inequivalentes sans\n","règle GVH supplémentaire dérivée, le postulat échoue au critère\n","d’origine unique.\n","\n","Falsificateur théorique F3 — limite GR non contrôlée\n","\n","Si le secteur proposé ne possède pas une limite régulière reproduisant\n","la branche GR exigée par la chaîne, il doit être rejeté comme fermeture\n","de cette branche GVH.\n","\n","Falsificateur observationnel F4 — PPN\n","\n","Une fois tau_G et sa dynamique fixés avant confrontation aux\n","données, la théorie devra produire des coefficients faibles et donc :\n","\n","$$\n","\\gamma_{\\rm GVH},\\qquad \\beta_{\\rm GVH}.\n","$$\n","\n","Si ces valeurs prédites sont incompatibles avec les contraintes\n","observationnelles utilisées par la phase de validation, la branche est\n","réfutée ou son espace de paramètres correspondant exclu.\n","\n","Ce test est particulièrement propre parce que 0.2.23.1 a déjà figé la\n","carte entre coefficients métriques et paramètres PPN.\n","\n","Falsificateur observationnel F5 — effets de référentiel préféré\n","\n","Si le choix dynamique de u^mu produit des effets de référentiel\n","préféré inévitables dépassant les limites observationnelles, la branche\n","correspondante est réfutée. Le prochain notebook doit dériver ces\n","observables à partir de l’action/équations choisies plutôt que les\n","introduire comme paramètres libres indépendants.\n","\n","Falsificateur observationnel F6 — anisotropie/source\n","\n","Puisque 0.2.23.2 identifie le canal Pi_mn[T] au stress anisotrope,\n","toute prédiction spécifique reliant le champ timelike à ce canal devra\n","être testée dans des systèmes où l’anisotropie est non nulle. Une\n","relation universelle annoncée par le futur postulat et absente des\n","données constituerait une réfutation.\n","\n","────────\n","\n","11. Condition minimale pour ouvrir 0.2.23.6\n","\n","0.2.23.6 ne doit être ouvert comme nouvelle étape physique que si\n","les éléments suivants sont écrits avant le fit :\n","\n",